course: dictionary
lesson: 9314
title: The speedometer
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A speedometer is the dial or screen in a vehicle that shows how fast it is going right now. The numbers or the moving needle tell you the speed.
explain: «Speed is how far you go in a certain time: when the car's speedometer shows 50, the car would cover 50 kilometres if it kept that speed for a whole hour.» So the number on the speedometer tells you how far you would go in one hour at that speed.
explain: Speed = distance ÷ time. A car that goes 120 kilometres in 2 hours has a speed of 60 kilometres per hour. Maths and science lessons use this to work out speed from a journey.
explain: Countries use different units. The UK and USA use miles per hour, while Canada, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland use kilometres per hour. Always check which unit your speedometer shows.
fact: A speedometer shows how fast a vehicle is going at this moment.
fact: You can find a speedometer in cars, bikes, trains and other vehicles.
fact: Speed is measured in miles per hour (UK and USA) or kilometres per hour (Canada, Australia, New Zealand, Ireland).
fact: Speed = distance ÷ time.
fact: Speed limits tell drivers the fastest they may go safely, so drivers check their speedometer to keep within them.
exercise: What does a speedometer show? | The total distance a vehicle has travelled | How much fuel is left in the tank | *How fast the vehicle is going | The number of passengers
exercise: A car goes 120 kilometres in 2 hours. What is its speed? | 122 kilometres per hour | 240 kilometres per hour | 2 kilometres per hour | *60 kilometres per hour
exercise: In which country would a speedometer show kilometres per hour? | *Australia | United States | United Kingdom
test: «When the car's speedometer shows 50, the car would cover 50 kilometres if it kept that speed for a whole hour.» How far would the car go in one hour at 50? | 50 metres | *50 kilometres | 5 kilometres | 500 kilometres
test: Why do road safety lessons remind drivers to check their speedometer? | *To keep to the speed limit | To count the passengers | To see what colour the car is | To find the nearest petrol station
exam: A car's speedometer shows 60 and it keeps that speed for 3 hours. How far does it go? | 600 kilometres | 20 kilometres | 63 kilometres | *180 kilometres
